claim.claim-text:
a frame (80) configured to be supported on a head of the user (90);
an image projector (930) coupled to the frame (80) and configured to project images into the user's eye (210) to display image content in the vision field of the user (90);
a camera (920) coupled to the frame (80);
a waveguide (940) coupled to the frame (80) and optically coupled to the camera (920);
an optical coupling optical element (944) coupled to the frame (80) and configured such that light is coupled into the waveguide (940);
an out-coupling element (952) coupled to the frame (80) and configured to direct light emitted from the waveguide (940) to the camera (920);
a first light source (934, 960) coupled to the frame (80) and configured to direct light to the user's eye (210); and
processing electronics (140) coupled to the first light source (934) and to the camera (920), the processing electronics (140) configured to control the camera (920) to capture images periodically, while pulsing the first light source (934) in time with the camera (920) image capture such that light emitted by the first light source (934) has a reduced intensity when the camera (920) is not capturing images.

a first diffractive optical element configured to couple light from the user's eye (210) into the waveguide (940);
a second diffractive optical element configured to couple light from the image projector (930) out of the waveguide (940) to the user's eye (210); and
a third diffractive optical element configured to couple light from the plurality of infrared light sources (934, 960) out of the waveguide (940) to the user's eye (210).

present a first virtual target for the user's eye (210) at a first known point of gaze such that the camera (920) captures a first retinal image at the first known point of gaze; and
after presenting the first virtual target, present a second virtual target for the user's eye (210) at a second known point of gaze, the camera (920) capturing a second retinal image at the second known point of gaze;
wherein the processing electronics (140) are configured to generate a mapping matrix of a retina of the user's eye (210) utilizing the first retinal image and the second retinal image.

projecting images into the user's eye (210), via the image projector (930), to display image content in the vision field of the user (90);
while projecting images into the user's eye (210), periodically capturing images utilizing the camera (920); and
controlling the first light source (934, 960) to pulse in time with the camera (920) such that light emitted by the first light source (934, 960) has a reduced intensity when the camera (920) is not capturing images
